The Arrival class member is the time that the Customer object enters the simulation.
To simplify matters, time will evolve in discrete (e.g., one minute) intervals and, hence,
Arrival will take on only integer values. The Gold class member represents the presence
or absence of “gold” status in the sense associated with car rentals, airlines, etc., where
frequent patronage can lead to a customer receiving a preferential “gold” level of service.
